    a: "Tags are key-value labels like Project, Env and Owner that I put on every resource, so I can find, automate and bill by them. The Resource Groups Tagging API finds everything with a given tag across services, and a resource group saves that query so I can view or act on the whole set. I activate the important keys as cost allocation tags so Cost Explorer can split the bill per project, and I enforce required tags with tag policies or IaC defaults instead of hoping people remember.",
    code: "aws ec2 create-tags --resources i-0abc123def4567890 \\\n    --tags Key=Project,Value=shop Key=Env,Value=prod\n\n# Everything for one project, across services\naws resourcegroupstaggingapi get-resources --tag-filters Key=Project,Values=shop \\\n    --query 'ResourceTagMappingList[].ResourceARN'\n\n# Save that query as a resource group\naws resource-groups create-group --name shop-prod \\\n    --resource-query file://shop-query.json --query 'Group.GroupArn'",
    output: "[\n    \"arn:aws:ec2:us-east-1:123456789012:instance/i-0abc123def4567890\",\n    \"arn:aws:s3:::example-shop-assets\",\n    \"arn:aws:lambda:us-east-1:123456789012:function:orders-api\",\n    \"arn:aws:dynamodb:us-east-1:123456789012:table/orders\"\n]\n\n\"arn:aws:resource-groups:us-east-1:123456789012:group/shop-prod\"",
