    q: "What is an Auto Scaling group?",
    level: 'Intermediate',
    a: "An Auto Scaling group keeps a fleet of EC2 instances between a min and max size, launched from a launch template across several AZs. It replaces unhealthy instances automatically and scales out or in with scaling policies. I usually use target tracking, like keeping average CPU at 50%, and I set the ASG health check to ELB so instances that fail the load balancer check get replaced too.",
    code: "aws autoscaling create-auto-scaling-group --auto-scaling-group-name web-asg \\\n    --launch-template LaunchTemplateName=web-lt \\\n    --min-size 2 --max-size 6 \\\n    --vpc-zone-identifier \"subnet-0cc33dd44ee55ff66,subnet-0dd44ee55ff66aa77\" \\\n    --target-group-arns $TG_ARN --health-check-type ELB\n\n# Target tracking: keep average CPU around 50%\naws autoscaling put-scaling-policy --auto-scaling-group-name web-asg \\\n    --policy-name cpu50 --policy-type TargetTrackingScaling \\\n    --target-tracking-configuration file://cpu50.json",
