    a: "API Gateway is a managed front door for APIs: it handles routing, auth (IAM, Cognito, Lambda authorizers), throttling, CORS and custom domains, and forwards requests to Lambda or other backends. With proxy integration my Lambda gets the whole request and must return statusCode, headers and a string body. I prefer HTTP APIs for simple Lambda backends because they are cheaper and faster than REST APIs.",
    code: "import json\n\n# API Gateway (Lambda proxy integration) handler\ndef lambda_handler(event, context):\n    user_id = event[\"pathParameters\"][\"id\"]\n    return {\n        \"statusCode\": 200,\n        \"headers\": {\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"},\n        \"body\": json.dumps({\"id\": user_id, \"name\": \"Sam\"}),\n    }",
