    q: "What is AWS Step Functions?",
    level: 'Intermediate',
    a: "Step Functions is a managed workflow service: I describe the steps as a state machine in JSON (Amazon States Language), and AWS runs them, passes data between them and keeps a visual history of every execution. Retries with backoff, error catching, parallel branches, waits and human approval steps are configuration instead of code. I use it when a process has several steps that can fail independently, like an order flow, instead of chaining Lambdas that call each other.",
