    a: "A Cognito user pool is a managed user directory: it handles sign-up, email verification, password policies, MFA, social logins and issues JWTs (ID, access and refresh tokens). The frontend logs in through the Amplify library or the hosted login page, then sends the access token as a Bearer header, and API Gateway's Cognito or JWT authorizer validates it before my Lambda runs. I never verify tokens by hand without checking the signature against the pool's JWKS, and I keep tokens short-lived.",
