    q: "What is the difference between RDS Multi-AZ and read replicas?",
    level: 'Intermediate',
    a: "Multi-AZ is for availability: RDS keeps a synchronous standby in another AZ and fails over automatically, usually in one to two minutes, but in the classic setup the standby doesn't serve traffic. Read replicas are for read scaling: they are asynchronous copies, possibly in other regions, with their own endpoint that my app sends read queries to, and they can lag a little behind. In production I use both: Multi-AZ for the primary, and replicas for reports or read-heavy pages, and I remember a replica can be promoted for DR.",
