    q: "How do you troubleshoot a Lambda timeout?",
    level: 'Advanced',
    a: "The default timeout is only 3 seconds (max 15 minutes), so first I check the logs for 'Task timed out' and the REPORT line to see duration and memory. Common causes are a slow downstream call, a Lambda in a VPC trying to reach the internet or AWS APIs without a NAT Gateway or VPC endpoint (it just hangs), or too little memory, since CPU scales with memory. I set SDK and HTTP client timeouts shorter than the function timeout so it fails fast with a clear error, and remember API Gateway's own integration timeout is 29 seconds by default.",
