    level: 'Advanced',
    a: "Organizations groups many AWS accounts under one management account, with organizational units (OUs), consolidated billing and policies applied from the top. An SCP is a guardrail on an OU or account: it sets the maximum permissions anyone there can have, even the account's root user, but it never grants anything by itself. I use SCPs for a few hard rules, like allowed regions, no leaving the organization and no disabling CloudTrail or GuardDuty, and test them on a sandbox OU first.",
