    q: "How do you design a multi-account strategy (landing zone, Control Tower)?",
    level: 'Advanced',
    a: "I separate workloads and environments into accounts, because an account is the strongest isolation boundary for security, quotas and billing. A typical landing zone has a management account used only for billing and Organizations, a Security OU with a log-archive and an audit account, and a Workloads OU with dev, staging and prod accounts per team, plus a Sandbox OU. Control Tower sets this up with SSO, centralized CloudTrail and Config, and preventive and detective controls, and its Account Factory creates new accounts with the same baseline; people log in through IAM Identity Center, never with IAM users.",
